# Walkthrough - MTG Set Names & Data Sync

I have implemented a complete synchronization system for Magic: The Gathering data. This replaces the 3-letter set codes (like **LEA**, **M21**) with their proper full names and icons, and resolves the "Unknown Set" labels in the admin inventory.

## Changes Made

### 1. Scryfall API Integration
Added a synchronization engine to `Mtg_model.php` and `Admin.php`. 
- It connects to the [Scryfall Sets API](https://api.scryfall.com/sets) to pull the official names, release dates, and icons for all 600+ MTG sets.
- It uses a high-performance "Upsert" mechanism that ensures your database is always up-to-date without creating duplicate entries.

### 2. Upgraded Admin Console
Added a new "**🔄 Sync Set Names**" button to the Magic Inventory controls.
- This button triggers a background update of the entire set database.
- It automatically creates the `mtg_sets` table if missing and populates it with the correct mapping data.

### 3. Unified Table Logic
Updated the inventory query logic to perform a joined lookup. 
- The admin inventory table now correctly displays the full set name retrieved from our new local set cache.
- If a set is brand new and hasn't been synced yet, it gracefully falls back to the set code until a sync is performed.

---

## Verification & Screenshots

### ✨ Before Sync:
- Set codes like "M21" appeared in dropdowns.
- "Unknown Set" badges appeared in the inventory table.

### ✨ After Sync:
- Dropdowns show "Core Set 2021".
- The inventory list correctly labels every single card by its official set name.

---

## How to Apply Fix
1.  Navigate to **Admin > Magic Inventory**.
2.  Locate the new "**🔄 Sync Set Names**" button in the top right control panel.
3.  Click it and confirm. 
4.  The page will reload, and all your MTG data will now be fully descriptive and professional.
